  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saving the Sumatran Elephant through Encroachment Reduction and Preventing Future Deforestation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to focus on the prevention of encroachment and protection of the habitat through patrol and direct monitoring in the field, specifically, (1) the reduction of encroachment and other threats in areas with key elephant populations, and (2) an improved understanding of deforestation predictions in areas under threats of deforestation. The study area focuses on Bukit Barisan Selatan and Gunung Leuser National Parks which form part of the Barisan mountain range, a series of volcanoes up to 3,800m which lie along the entire western edge of the island of Sumatra.</narrative>
  </description>
